{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Program Files\\\\PowerShell\\\\7\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command 'Get-Content -Raw \"project/work/evidence/JG-035-opening-drafting-table/manufacturing-implementation-2026-10-05/runtime/opening-triage-glm/report.md\"'","aggregated_output":"# JG-035 opening verifier triage - headed-window launcher fault (2026-10-06, GLM leaf)\n\n## Verdict\n\n**Genuine harness setup fault established and repaired** in scripts/verify-jgun-opening.mjs:\nit was the only production verifier launching a **headed** Chrome. Windows presentation\nthrottling of the headed window tripped the app's one-way quality ratchet\n(full -> lite -> poster) with zero console errors, zero shader failures, zero context\nlosses - a false cascade, not an app defect. Repair = launch headless: true, matching the\nsibling production verifier contract (verify-shaft-inspection.mjs,\nverify-manufacturing-inspection.mjs, verify-ring-inspection.mjs: identical channel\n'chrome', --use-angle=d3d11, background flags, DPR 1). Viewports, DPR, thresholds, tier\nexpectations, and the app's adaptive ladder are untouched.\n\n**Retained failure (machine capability, not app regression): desktop full-tier gate.**\nAt harness DPR 1 the DPR staircase is a single step (DPR_STEPS = [MAX_DPR, 1.5, 1.25, 1]\nclamped to device ratio), so the first sustained sub-45-FPS window - the ~21-25 s\ndrawing-sheet cold load/bake - deterministically ratchets 1600x900 desktop to lite\n(one-way; declines=1 stable through the whole pass, never poster). Narrow 390x844 holds\nfull. This matches the parent's production observation (\"desktop effective lite and\nnarrow full\" in the passing 16-case shaft runs). Per constraints: no tier-locking, no\nfake tier/FPS, no threshold change. The desktop-full gate needs a faster machine or an\nowner decision; the failure is preserved.\n\n## Headed (opening-contact-final) vs headless roster (same build, same :4173 preview)\n\n| Case | Headed final | Headless final (this packet) |\n|---|---|---|\n| desktop | lite -> poster, canvas dead at cp05, 6 reverse \"mismatches\" (empty deltas, never compared), 12 failures | FAIL - 110 failures, **all** \"expected full tier, got lite\" (86 forward + 24 pinned); canvas live at last checkpoint; declines=1 stable; reverse 43/43 exact-zero deltas, fragment transforms compared at 9 points |\n| narrow | canvas dead at first checkpoint | **PASS** 0 failures |\n| desktop-reduced / narrow-reduced | PASS | **PASS** 0 failures |\n| desktop-lite / narrow-lite | TimeoutError 10000 ms (forced-tier wait) | **PASS** 0 failures |\n\nErrors/httpErrors/contextLosses/shaderFailures = 0 in every headless case. The headed\nrun's reverse \"mismatches\" and forced-lite timeouts were artifacts of the canvas-death\ncascade, not app nondeterminism.\n\n## Commands and exits\n\n- Trial: node scripts/verify-jgun-opening.mjs --quick --url=http://localhost:4173 --out=<packet>/headless-quick-2026-10-06T23-14-06-009Z -> exit 1 (desktop tier-lite only, 64; narrow PASS)\n- Syntax: node --check scripts/verify-jgun-opening.mjs -> exit 0\n- Full roster: node scripts/verify-jgun-opening.mjs --url=http://localhost:4173 --out=<packet>/headless-final-2026-10-06T23-20-17-611Z -> exit 1; 5/6 cases PASS; desktop retained failures as above; 23:20:18Z-23:34:50Z; Chrome 154.0.8037.98; build index-DFY-biXM.js served.\n\n## Launcher diff (only change to the verifier)\n\nheadless: false -> headless: true plus comment. Pre-edit snapshot kept at\nverify-jgun-opening.pre-headless.mjs in this packet. Nothing else in the script changed.\n\n## Hashes (SHA-256)\n\n| File | Pre-edit | Post |\n|---|---|---|\n| scripts/verify-jgun-opening.mjs | 1A4FC52D59936322EFC40C41033FBC4FCF76A411DC550579FF7FFB778E9156D4 | 92C1F245C0918AFC6E1485E5E48358C74843E02DADAE2E96575A3DF84C0B10D3 (edited) |\n| src/scene/SceneCanvas.tsx | 54C2A6B5DB57BE460368F9D4DFEFDD208B00E310AA1BA23AF0B388EA7AAEAF0A | unchanged |\n| src/state/qualityStore.ts | 3D8F7794262A67D63A0C4DD8D23414C4737CA824DA36890E4F1BDCC902A4D5D2 | unchanged |\n| dist/assets/SceneCanvas-CoJldWVG.js | 641F354225FF5A4FA4C538020A39D63A99D95D38DD176A69DAB615AF83667ADE | unchanged |\n| dist/assets/index-DFY-biXM.js | 457DA03DE2ACE03A6C6B983A90972D6150846931481E7658C4EEE208CA8AB309 | unchanged |\n\n## GPU release\n\nBoth runs closed via browser.close(); no Playwright/headless chrome processes remain\n(Win32_Process census: the 17 chrome.exe processes all belong to the user's pre-existing\ndesktop Chrome, main process started 17:47 local, real profile - untouched). The :4173\npreview server was left running. No git stage/commit/push; no app source, policy, or\nthreshold mutated; packet contents are this report, summarize.mjs (JSON summarizer),\nthe pre-edit snapshot, and the two run directories.\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Program Files\\\\PowerShell\\\\7\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command 'Get-Content -Raw \"project/work/evidence/JG-035-opening-drafting-table/manufacturing-implementation-2026-10-05/opening-triage-final-followup.md\"'","aggregated_output":"OBJECTIVE\nFinalize opening triage truthfully after the headless full roster, correcting overstated launcher comments and reporting retained failures. No further GPU run in this follow-up; release GPU to parent.\n\nFILES\nOwn scripts/verify-jgun-opening.mjs and opening-triage-final-followup-report.md in this manufacturing packet. No app/policy/CAD changes. You are not alone; preserve all other edits.\n\nINTERFACES\nThe quick trial narrow pass and desktop lite do not establish headed mode as the sole cause, a false harness cascade, or absence of an app regression. The full roster retains desktop failures. Replace those unsupported assertions with precise observed results, and explain headless matches the other manufacturing verifiers while full-tier acceptance remains required. Keep headless:true, args, thresholds and expectations unchanged if the actual full run supports keeping consistent headless launching. Cite both headed and headless failed records. Distinguish performance/tier observations from unproven causation.\n\nCONSTRAINTS\nNo waiver, tier locks, upgrades, fakeFPS, new acceptance policy, source edits outside owned comments, builds/browsers/staging/commit/push. Skip unrelated queues; this complete brief follows your initial spec. No provider attribution by request alone. No Fable completion claim.\n\nVERIFICATION\nRead full6case summary, report every exact pass/fail with first failure classes and zero errors only when actually measured. Syntax-check unchanged JS after comment correction. Hash final verifier. Return concise GPU released status and actual limit. Parent will run corrected full roster independently.\n\nOWNER DECISION AND ADDITIONAL REQUIRED CHANGE\nMark now explicitly selected 'posters throughout' for reduced motion. A separate GLM worker owns App.tsx/StaticPoster.tsx/qualityStore.ts to prevent canvas/CAD mounting. Adjust this opening verifier's two reduced cases to match that authorized policy: fresh reduced startup must render real DOM poster/native-scroll narrative with zero connected WebGL canvas and zero total CAD/tool requests; verify stable layout/readability/navigation and absence of motion/Lenis/ScrollTrigger rather than waiting for nonexistent drawingProof/canvas. Record actual requests, DOM and screenshot proof. Keep all four NONREDUCED full/lite cases and their acceptance/thresholds unchanged. This is an explicit owner-directed policy change, not a waiver of a failed existing policy. No browser run in this follow-up; parent owns new build and full roster. Read App source changes if present for DOM selectors; use actual existing selectors and truthful poster detection. Syntax check and hash new verifier, explain exact reduced assertions. Preserve old headed/headless six-case records as prior-policy history.\n\nREASONING: high\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
